{"title":"dosing the poison cure, scorpio ii","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/dosing-the-poison-cure-scorpio-ii","date":1762328160000,"content":"<figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2691\" height=\"1514\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/56592cd0-5c4d-4edb-bf03-b69501965c2a/scorpio_ii.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n \n\n\n  <p><em>this series of illustrations and writings are from my collaboration with </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\"><em>LJ of Ceremony</em></a><em> for their communal writing practice, </em><a href=\"https://www.ceremony-studio.co.uk/atmospheres\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Atmospheres</em></a><em>, based of the 36 decans of the astrological year. </em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p><strong>Scorpio II</strong> — 1 November – 11 November<br /><strong>Key themes from LJ</strong> — nostalgia, symbiosis, healing<br /><strong>Before this: </strong><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/hunger-for-a-creative-feast-scorpio-i\">hunger for a creative feast, scorpio i<br /></a><br />*</p><p>without realizing it, I gave myself two dosages ofthe poison cure during the ten day window of this decan. the first was when I visited a snake sanctuary and held a snake in my arms, and felt startled by how much peace I felt. </p><p>the second was when I bungee jumped off a bridge, and accompanied my body as it cycled through through the sensations of terror, exhilaration, and cosmic rebirth. both experiences felt like receiving a tiny dose of poison — it was anxiety inducing, and, it was healing, empowering, medicinal. it felt like a sort of vaccine from fear — it showed me what was on the other side of my fear: <em>joy, peace, spaciousness.</em>  <br /></p><p>while illustrating this decan, I grappled with how nostalgia and memory create such a tempting, seductive potion. sometimes I catch myself in it — not necessarily romanticizing the past, but swimming around in its depths and drowning in its gold liquid. sometimes writing feels like this. but grief and loss is, itself, a poison cure. to write about things that bring me pain is its own kind of excorcism — releasing the venom of experience. and, it also feels like healing. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n <hr />\n\n\n  <h1>process</h1>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n  